message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it as below."
title: "ACS Framework (Asymmetric Codependent Systems)"
abstract: >-
  Canonical manuscripts, mathematical notes, verification suites, and
  reproduction harnesses for the Asymmetric Codependent Systems (ACS)
  theoretical framework, representing approximately 5,000-6,000 hours of
  novel independent research by Bradley Wallace. All novel theories and
  hypotheses originated solely with the author, who navigates dyslexia
  and ADHD and utilized a human-in-the-loop Analog Mixture-of-Experts
  AI ensemble (GPT, Claude, Grok, DeepSeek, Gemini, Cursor, Antigravity)
  for voice-driven intake, transcription, and multi-model cross-examination.
  All claims are tracked under a four-tier verification hierarchy.
type: software
authors:
